From 444a618460840ddd9ec64338180793e341ab0a15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phillipxh <150742483+Phillipxh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:22:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): sign in with Home Assistant

Home Assistant speaks OAuth 2.0 but not OpenID Connect (no discovery, no
ID token, no userinfo), so it cannot be used as OIDC_ISSUER. With
HOMEASSISTANT_URL set, the existing SSO flow uses Home Assistant as its
source instead: authorize with PKCE, code exchange, the user is read via
the WebSocket API (auth/current_user) and the refresh token is revoked
right away. Linking, OIDC_ALLOW_SIGNUP, SSO-only accounts,
AUTH_ALLOW_PASSWORD_LOGIN and the second factor apply unchanged. A
configured OIDC provider takes precedence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019TNUHVPEM9ZvMaCtSc7RP5
Signed-off-by: Phillipxh <150742483+Phillipxh@users.noreply.github.com>
